  "instance_name": "historical_ku_klan_violence",
  "label": "Historical Ku Klux Klan violence against Black Americans",
  "description": "The Ku Klux Klan was a white supremacist terrorist organization in the United States that engaged in violent acts, including lynchings, against Black people, particularly during the Reconstruction era and into the 20th century. The statistic of 3,446 Black people killed over 86 years refers to documented lynchings and other racially motivated killings attributed to the KKK and related white supremacist groups. This requires external historical knowledge to understand the context and scale of the violence depicted by the visual of the KKK members.",
